msgid "Keepmerge – Push Staging to Live"
msgstr ""

#. Description of the plugin
#: keepmerge-push-staging-to-live.php
msgid "Pushes content and media from staging to live with a dry-run diff, conflict checks and rollback. Code is reported, never pushed."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
#: keepmerge-push-staging-to-live.php
msgid "SoftGlaze"
msgstr ""

#. Author URI of the plugin
#: keepmerge-push-staging-to-live.php
msgid "https://softglaze.com"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-menu.php:37
msgid "Staging Push"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-menu.php:62
msgid "Push content and data from staging to live and keep what changed on live. Theme and plugin code is reported, never pushed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-menu.php:69
msgid "This screen needs JavaScript. Turn it on in your browser to use Keepmerge."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-privacy.php:32
msgid "This site uses Keepmerge to move content between this site and another WordPress site owned by the same administrator (usually a staging copy and the live site). Transfers happen only between those two sites, only after an administrator paired them, and only when an administrator starts an action. No data is sent to SoftGlaze or to any other third party."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-privacy.php:33
msgid "Keepmerge keeps an audit log of pairing, push and rollback activity. Each entry can include the user ID of the administrator who acted and the IP address of the request, including the address of the paired site. Audit entries are kept for 180 days by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-privacy.php:34
msgid "Before a push changes an item, the receiving site stores a snapshot of that item so the push can be rolled back. Snapshots are kept for 30 days by default (and for at least the three most recent pushes). Pushed content and snapshots can contain personal data that is already part of the site's content, such as names in posts or pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-privacy.php:35
msgid "Keepmerge never reads or transfers user accounts, comments, orders or customer records."
msgstr ""

